  "worked_solution": "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\sqrt{6÷(6-{2}^{2})} & = \\\\ 7\\sqrt{6÷(6-4)} & = \\\\ 7\\sqrt{6÷2} & = \\\\ 7\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
